WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Episode 555.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.900
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.280
Today is July 28th, 2026.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.180
Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:20.020
Tesla locked in 90% of an Arizona Solar Plus storage project to power its growing AI inference

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.500
clusters.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:32.260
Tesla began pushing FSD-V14 light version 2022, 0.20.6.11, to a larger share of HW3 cars in

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.780
the United States and Canada.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.640
The update came after a bug fix point release following a limited wave that started on July

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.320
21.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:50.300
It merges firmware with the HW4 branch at 2026.20.6.11, giving HW3 cars the latest

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.060
distilled features available on newer hardware.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:01:00.140
Roughly 18% of the HW3 fleet in the US and Canada had received the update by the latest

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.160
tracking snapshot.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:08.780
HW3 vehicles will still trail HW4 capability due to compute limits on the larger model.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.880
Owners outside North America continue to wait for the update.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:22.300
Tesla's head of AI had previously announced version 2026.20.6.10, before the quick bug

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.320
fix iteration.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.360
Now the focus shifts from software progress on existing vehicles to the production headaches

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.360
still constraining new hardware like the Cybertruck.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:38.520
Tesla filed suit against the Cybertruck component supplier that is allegedly withholding tooling

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.240
and holding production hostage.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.720
The dispute centers on owned dies and fixtures the supplier refuses to release without additional

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.600
daily payments.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.500
Production of the vehicle remains constrained while the legal process plays out.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:58.700
The supplier is accused of demanding ongoing fees to hand over equipment that Tesla already

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.160
owns.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.940
That manufacturing constraint highlights Tesla's broader need for reliable power at scale.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:11.540
Tesla has locked in 90% of the output from a KKR backed solar and battery installation

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.400
in Arizona to support its expanding inference workloads.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:21.700
The deal reflects the shift from GPU stockpiling to securing megawatts of dedicated renewable

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.540
capacity.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.760
Construction and interconnection timelines will determine when the power reaches Cortex

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.260
clusters.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.840
Danny Nas noted the 90% commitment in recent coverage.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.700
The project adds to earlier long-term power agreements Tesla has signed in the same state.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.860
Tesla and Zillestra finalized a multi-year power purchase agreement for solar generation

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:45.500
in Texas.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.980
The contract adds dedicated renewable supply to support both vehicle manufacturing and energy

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.280
storage operations at Giga, Texas.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.360
Details on capacity and pricing remain undisclosed.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.620
A separate report from renews confirmed the same Texas solar PPA signing.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:09.420
The agreement aligns with Tesla's broader push to pair solar generation with on-site storage

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:09.880
needs.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:15.580
That power deal leads naturally into a closer look at why megawatts are becoming the new

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:16.380
bottleneck.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.180
Power constraints now shape AI development more directly than chip counts.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.980
Tesla's decision to secure the bulk of an Arizona Solar Plus storage project shows the company

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.720
treating megawatts as a scarce input that must be locked in years ahead of demand.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.560
The move mirrors how data center operators once raced for substations rather than servers.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:45.440
Securing dedicated renewable output also reduces exposure to utility rate volatility that can

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.800
swing inference costs unpredictably.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.060
Traditional utilities plan generation around predictable load growth curves.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:59.020
Tesla's inference clusters create bursty high density demand that existing grids were

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.100
not size to serve at short notice.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.600
By contracting directly for dedicated renewable capacity, the company bypasses interconnection

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.980
cues that can stretch three to five years for new transmission.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.000
The Arizona project therefore functions as both a capacity hedge and a timing advantage.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.980
The economics hinge on whether the secured power delivers lower effective cost per inference

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:28.480
token than buying from the spot market or relying on grid upgrades paid for by all rate

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:28.960
payers.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:35.200
Deutsche Bank lowered its Tesla price target after concluding that unsupervised robot taxi

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.640
progress has lagged internal timelines.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.460
The revision reflects slower regulatory and deployment milestones than previously modeled.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.420
Investors now await clearer production and approval dates.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:54.160
The bank specifically flagged lagging robot taxi advancement as the primary reason for the adjustment.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:05:01.000
That analyst adjustment arrives as investors press for proof that Tesla's AI pivot will generate

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:08.000
returns. Analysts and shareholders want clear unit economics on the shift from vehicles to autonomy

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:14.300
and robotics. Coverage emphasizes that the company's valuation now rests heavily on future

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:21.020
AI revenue streams rather than current auto margins. Recent earnings highlighted continued spending

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:27.440
without corresponding near-term monetization. The market is watching for the first material external

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:33.740
contracts or fleet deployments. The gap between investment pays and visible revenue remains the

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:39.720
central point of discussion. Post-earning stock weakness raises questions about next steps.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:45.740
Tesla shares fell after the latest results prompting discussion on whether the company needs to

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:53.240
accelerate non-auto programs or defend vehicle margins. Commentary focuses on the gap between heavy AI

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:59.960
and robotics investment and current cash generation. Some observers argue the valuation already

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:06.720
prices in successful robot taxi and optimist outcomes. The next earnings update is expected to provide

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:13.300
more granular spending guidance. The post earnings drop has left investors recalibrating expectations

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:20.620
for the balance between near-term auto results and longer-term AI bets. BYD announced its initial

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:26.320
humanoid robot will be unveiled next month, directly entering the space Tesla has targeted with

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:32.340
optimists. The Chinese automakers move adds another competitor to the race for low-cost general

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:39.260
purpose humanoids. No production timeline or target applications were disclosed. The debut is

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:45.500
positioned as a direct response to Tesla's ongoing optimist development. While competitors line up,

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:52.280
Tesla's own robotics effort just took a small external step forward. Vertwix completed its first

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:58.380
sale of specialized hardware to Tesla's Optimus program as part of an expanding AI and robotics

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:04.400
strategy. The transaction marks an early external supplier relationship for the humanoid effort.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:11.540
Further volume or integration details were not released. The sale advances Vertwix's stated push into

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:17.980
robotics hardware alongside its existing virtual reality products. External supplier momentum

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:25.120
contrasts with the internal timeline warnings now coming from Musk himself. Elon Musk stated that both the

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.940
Robotaxi and humanoid robot programs face meaningful remaining hurdles before commercial scale.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:37.380
The comments temper earlier expectations for near-term unsupervised deployment and volume production.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.420
Investors are watching for updated milestones in upcoming earnings commentary.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:48.680
The remarks came in response to questions about whether current development pace matches prior public

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:55.420
targets. Timeline caution pairs with fresh questions about how hard the FSD team has been pushed

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:01.260
to meet those targets. Court filings quote a former Tesla manager stating that self-driving

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:06.860
vehicle engineers were pushed so hard that test cars became rolling hazards on public roads.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:13.260
The complaint alleges excessive hours and inadequate oversight during rapid iteration cycles.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:20.400
Tesla has not yet responded publicly to the specific claims. The manager described vehicles

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.820
operating without sufficient validation before being placed on public streets.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:30.180
Internal pressure stories sit alongside a new federal look at hardware safety.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:37.340
US regulators launched a broad investigation into flush door handle designs after multiple Tesla models

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:43.780
raised concerns about emergency exit performance. The review covers vehicle egress under power

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:49.080
loss and crash conditions. Tesla has not disclosed any planned hardware changes.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.660
The probe examines whether the handles meet federal requirements for manual operation when

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:01.200
primary power systems fail. Regulatory scrutiny on existing vehicles rounds out a week that also

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:07.920
brought smaller but tangible customer updates. Reddit users posted photos of a cyber cab prototype

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:14.300
fitted with a conventional steering wheel, suggesting ongoing development of a manually operable version.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:21.060
The images indicate Tesla is exploring retrofit paths for regulatory or testing flexibility.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:27.280
No official confirmation has been issued. The modifications appear on vehicles originally shown

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:33.440
without steering wheels at the Wii robot event. Tesla opened immediate delivery slots for the

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:40.040
six-seat Model Y variant in Australia after earlier allocation limits. The configuration adds a third

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:46.340
row bench to the existing five-seat platform. Local pricing and availability windows remain listed

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:52.280
on the configurator. The move follows earlier production adjustments that had restricted the six-seat

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:58.880
option in certain markets. The in-car assistant now supports expanded multilingual interaction

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:04.300
directly through the vehicle interface. Tesla highlighted that GROC can handle more languages

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:10.940
and sits more tightly inside the car's systems than before. The change broadens accessibility for

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:16.960
non-English speakers without requiring phone pairing. Early users report smoother voice command

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:23.540
handling in mixed language households. The update builds on prior GROC voice features already present

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:29.960
in the infotainment stack. Cross-country records are now tracked by elapsed time rather than whether

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:35.940
the drive is feasible. Tesla noted that the supervised system has advanced to the point where the

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:42.980
limiting factor is speed, not capability. Community drivers are already posting new benchmark attempts.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.980
The shift shows how normalized long-distance autonomy has become for owners.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:54.220
Record attempts now focus on shaving minutes rather than proving the route can be completed at all.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:11:01.800
FSD supervise now feels ordinary to many owners. Tesla observed that the technology has crossed into

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:08.660
the background of ownership similar to other once-noble conveniences. Owners report relying on it for

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:14.000
routine commutes without second thought. The shift marks a quiet milestone in adoption.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:20.100
The feature now blends into everyday driving the way automatic transmissions once did for an earlier

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:26.540
generation. Court documents quote a former manager describing engineers working such extreme hours

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:33.340
that test vehicles posed hazards on public roads. The claims point to pressure from aggressive iteration

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:39.660
schedules and limited oversight. Tesla has not yet addressed the specific allegations in the filing.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:45.820
The manager's statements describe vehicles being released for public testing before adequate validation

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:52.080
cycles could be completed under the reported workload. Keep an eye on any updates from the federal

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:59.060
probe into door handles as more details emerge. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news. TSLA

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:10.080
closed at $304.86 down $4.36 1.4. If you enjoyed this episode please leave a rating or review.

